\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The two-axis experimental design. The identical pipeline is evaluated over a grid of \emph  {telemetry completeness} (C1--C4, horizontal; each a superset of the previous) and \emph  {learning paradigm} (static / periodic / online, vertical). RQ1 reads detection along the completeness axis (on the drifted stream, with the static row as a held-out reference) and RQ2 reads localisation on that reference; RQ3 sweeps the whole grid on the drifted stream as the regimes $R_0\!\rightarrow \!R_3$ shift the distribution.}}{11}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
